// THE WILDERNESS FISHING SPOTS (13 October, moved east 15 October). Suggestion #10 asked for raw
// manta and sea turtle in the Wilderness by the dragons; until then both fish came from the Fishing
// Trawler and nowhere else - the skill guide said so out loud and the Fishing level-up messages at
// 79 and 81 told the player as much.
//
// WHERE (moved 15 October). Four spots on the water east and north-east of the EAST dragons:
// (3384,3676) and (3385,3687) on the east coast, Wilderness 20 and 21, and (3370,3715) and
// (3373,3719) on the straight shore of the northern arm, Wilderness 25. They were first put in the
// pond among the WEST dragons, then on a patch of `water_no_texture` - which paints flat dull
// ground, carries no collision and is not what anyone means by the water out here - and then on the
// shoreline tiles of the real water, where they still looked wrong.
//
// A SHORELINE TILE IS HALF LAND. The water overlay (o6) comes in two kinds: whole tiles, written
// plain, and the beach tiles that cut a tile diagonally, written o6;shape;rotation. An npc draws at
// the centre of its tile, and the centre of a diagonal beach tile IS the waterline - which is
// exactly how it looked in game, bubbles sitting on the sand. These four stand on WHOLE water
// tiles, so the bubbles are in the blue.
//
// THAT IS WHY THERE ARE ONLY FOUR AND WHY THEY ARE IN TWO PAIRS. A whole water tile is no use
// unless a player can stand beside it, and the engine's reach for an npc is orthogonal only
// (reachedEntity -> rsmod.reached with shape -2; no diagonals). Along this entire coast between
// Wilderness 20 and 25 there are exactly six tiles that are whole water AND have a walkable
// neighbour sharing an edge, and all six were flood-filled back to a green dragon tile to prove
// they are not on a stranded piece of shore. These are four of them.
//
// STILL STATIC: moverestrict=nomove and wanderrange=0, as every other spot in this build. A fishing
// spot that drifts is a fishing spot nobody can click twice; spread along a shoreline is what makes
// this read as a shoal, and it costs the player nothing.

[wildyfish]
name=Fishing spot
desc=I can see something big swimming in the water.
model1=compofishspot_8
vislevel=hide
readyanim=fishingspot_ready
walkanim=fishingspot_walk
minimap=no
op3=Harpoon
op5=hidden
wanderrange=0
moverestrict=nomove
category=wildyfish
